{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "0be33911-c498-471e-9528-0252a57b7334",
		"name": "Imalo Education API",
		"description": "Full API coverage for the Imalo Education API (.NET 10 / ASP.NET Core Web API — see ai_docs/api.md). Import this collection plus the companion environment file (optional — a sane default baseUrl is baked in as a collection variable, so this works immediately after import even with no environment selected).\n\n**No authentication** — unlike some sibling projects, this API has no login/JWT flow (see ai_docs/api.md's Gotchas), so every request here runs unauthenticated by design.\n\n**Folders:**\n- **Scholars** — a numbered, top-to-bottom, self-cleaning walk through create → get → update → list → audit log → delete → confirm-gone. Safe to run repeatedly (Collection Runner-friendly): each pass creates and then deletes its own randomly-generated scholar.\n- **Attendance** — a self-contained, self-cleaning walk through a helper scholar's attendance: save → get-for-scholar → get-all → delete → cleanup.\n- **Audit Log** — the global (cross-scholar) paginated audit trail, plus the destructive clear-all-logs action.\n- **Negative & Edge Cases** — validation failures (`400`) and not-found (`404`) cases matching the status-code conventions documented in ai_docs/api.md and ai_docs/database.md. A couple of these register their own short-lived helper scholar first (same pattern as the other folders) and clean it up afterwards.\n- **Health** — the unauthenticated `/health` liveness check.\n\nSee `ai_docs/index.md` for the full architecture and `ai_docs/api.md` / `ai_docs/database.md` for the validation rules and status-code conventions this collection exercises.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"event": [
		{
			"listen": "test",
			"script": {
				"type": "text/javascript",
				"exec": [
					"pm.test(\"No unhandled server error (500)\", function () {",
					"    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.not.equal(500);",
					"});",
					"",
					"pm.test(\"Response time is reasonable (< 5s)\", function () {",
					"    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(5000);",
					"});"
				]
			}
		}
	],
